course: dictionary
lesson: 6128
title: Midwinter: a word about time and place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Midwinter means the middle of winter, the coldest and darkest part of the year. It is a noun (the midwinter) and an adjective (midwinter nights). Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The stones of Stonehenge line up with the sunrise in midsummer and the sunset in midwinter.» Midsummer is the middle of summer, so midwinter must be its opposite, the middle of winter.
explain: The clues in a sentence can tell you more than one thing. Midwinter is also the winter solstice, the shortest day of the year. In the northern half of the world that day falls in late December, but in the southern half it falls in June. So the same word can point to a different month depending on where you live.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «North of the Arctic Circle the sun does not rise for weeks in midwinter, because the Earth is tilted.» If you swap in "the shortest day of the year", the sentence still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
fact: Midwinter means the middle of winter, the coldest and darkest part of the year.
fact: Midwinter is also the winter solstice, the shortest day of the year.
fact: The winter solstice is in late December in the northern half of the world, and in June in the southern half.
fact: In science, midwinter is when one half of the Earth tilts furthest away from the Sun, so the days are shortest.
fact: Many festivals, such as Christmas, Yule and Hanukkah, come near midwinter in the north.
exercise: «North of the Arctic Circle the sun does not rise for weeks in midwinter, because the Earth is tilted.» What does midwinter mean here? | The middle of the night | The first warm day of spring | A summer picnic in the park | *The coldest, darkest part of winter
exercise: «The stones of Stonehenge line up with the sunrise in midsummer and the sunset in midwinter.» Find and copy the word that is the opposite of midwinter. | Stonehenge | sunrise | stones | *midsummer
exercise: Ella in Sydney says midwinter is in June, but Sam in London says it is in December. Why are they both right? | Midwinter is in the middle of summer | Midwinter is always in December, everywhere on Earth | *In the southern half of the world, the shortest day comes in June | In the southern half of the world, midwinter is in December
test: «Bear cubs are born in the den in midwinter, tiny and blind.» What does midwinter tell us about when the cubs are born? | In the first warm week of spring | *In the coldest, darkest part of winter | In the middle of a summer holiday
test: Which festival comes near midwinter in the north? | A summer picnic | Easter | *Christmas
exam: What is the best meaning of midwinter for a pupil? | The middle of summer, which is the longest day of the year | *The middle of winter, which is also the shortest day of the year | The end of the school term | The first snow of the year
